# WFORMTE.KEY - the layout grid, the Tab order through every field type
# and PgUp and PgDn in the form of every type in FORM_EDIT, PgUp past a
# disabled first field in FORM_VIEW; TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WFORMTE.SNP.
# The controls stand in the table's order, label then control, and the
# focus starts on the first field that can be changed.
K F5
S OPEN
# Tab visits each control of the Record page that takes the focus, in
# the table's order: edit controls, the check box, the drop-down lists,
# the read-only fields ID and SERIAL (FF_NEWONLY outside FORM_NEW), the
# password control, then the two buttons and the tab strip, and wraps.
# The memo, on the Notes page, is not shown.
K TAB
S CODE
K TAB
S QTY
K TAB
S PRICE
K TAB
S DATE
K TAB
S FLAG
K TAB
S STATUS
K TAB
S COND
K TAB
S ID
K TAB
S SERIAL
K TAB
S PASS
K TAB
S OK
K TAB
S CANCEL
K TAB
S STRIP
K TAB
S WRAP
# Shift-Tab goes the other way round.
K STAB
S BACKSTRP
K STAB
S BACKCAN
K STAB
S BACKOK
# On the Notes page PgUp from a button goes to the memo, then scrolls
# it, the focus staying there; elsewhere, a button too, PgUp and PgDn go
# to the first field shown, TEXT, and the last, PASS.
K CTRL-TAB PGUP
S MEMO
K PGUP
S MEMOPGUP
K CTRL-TAB
K PGUP
S PGUP
K PGDN
S PGDN
K TAB
K PGUP
S BTNPGUP
# Nothing was changed: Esc leaves without asking.
K ESC
S END
# PgDn on a closed drop-down list goes to the last field; on an open one
# it pages the list, which stays open, the focus on it.
K F5 ALT-S PGDN
S CBPGDN
K ALT-S ALT-DOWN PGDN
S LISTPGDN
# The password form in FORM_VIEW, its Notes page shown: PgUp from the
# Edit button passes over PASS, its first field, disabled and on the
# Record page, to NOTES, the first shown that takes the focus.
K ALT-UP ESC Y SHIFT-F1 CTRL-TAB STAB PGUP
S VIEWPGUP
K ESC
